{"id": "EUVD-2026-103613", "enisaUuid": "284affdf-cbb2-3a7c-a209-c07661056f47", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: use one headroom snapshot for neighbour replies\n\nvxlan_na_create() samples LL_RESERVED_SPACE() to size the reply skb and then\nsamples it again to reserve headroom. A concurrent vxlan_changelink() can\nupdate needed_headroom between the two reads, creating a TOCTOU race. The\nsecond value can exceed the allocation and make the Ethernet header write out\nof bounds.\n\nThe race is reproducible on the unpatched kernel. It occurred when\nvxlan_na_create() generated a neighbour reply while vxlan_changelink() changed\nthe link headroom. KASAN caught a four-byte write two bytes beyond a 704-byte\nskbuff_small_head allocation.\n\nSnapshot the headroom once and use that value for both allocation and\nreservation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45a67662bf8ce3aa5643accf98d328dfbb47eaf6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/315d42ca39f69846662961c25dcf2bb07c350d14", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3c5eb6e382dd426a5e7eb08608897ed57167ff7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff022fd9d0f0282c575e11778b96bd1b637503eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/481506a756dcd828ef42391cb08f38d8d96d38fc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98568", "GHSA-489c-q3cc-mm5r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0616d9db-f24e-3042-8bef-ddd0e7e9dff4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b29dba9c085a4fb79058fb1c45a2f6257ca3dfa <45a67662bf8ce3aa5643accf98d328dfbb47eaf6"}, {"id": "0777ae8f-f7ad-3d3c-b374-51d3cad4b81e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "5a891532-6d7e-3c56-a83a-f29f5cb66c44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3927dace523706cc00f808520eaf2125dd7c07b5"}, {"id": "5cecc0f7-988a-3a4d-a003-697e8b78bcb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b29dba9c085a4fb79058fb1c45a2f6257ca3dfa <315d42ca39f69846662961c25dcf2bb07c350d14"}, {"id": "67b905c3-d5f3-3ee5-9d9d-b358b3f08798", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.13.10 <3.14"}, {"id": "78607f90-f906-3731-b1d7-6bff751acd81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b29dba9c085a4fb79058fb1c45a2f6257ca3dfa <481506a756dcd828ef42391cb08f38d8d96d38fc"}, {"id": "9bcc9f9b-e2c4-3369-b871-0ecc9d795e97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.14"}, {"id": "af4b54a1-970a-3bb3-9b36-e4b9ab5e7d4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "be23ebc7-972c-389d-bdaf-2bbbf6c50ccc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d8be18c52dbc94989f6d74637b731af39cd3d902"}, {"id": "bf7487db-ada4-322f-aca1-4e73a52a3620", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "cafb82f0-3606-30bc-8410-0cda3abc3047", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d4f1616d-9a0a-31b0-839b-690273ea72b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b29dba9c085a4fb79058fb1c45a2f6257ca3dfa <ff022fd9d0f0282c575e11778b96bd1b637503eb"}, {"id": "f4ec2c8b-262e-33e0-8c8e-de4403649b62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b29dba9c085a4fb79058fb1c45a2f6257ca3dfa <a3c5eb6e382dd426a5e7eb08608897ed57167ff7"}, {"id": "f8e05ae3-c66a-34a6-bcef-4719dc44a027", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "fda79a6b-2461-3a40-a720-dd9b69b90e58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version"